invariant: INV-41
file: src/rsa_mont_division.h
catches: rsa_equiv_test_compare
reason: times_r_mod runs k - 1 steps of the division where R = 2^(64k)
  needs k, so the squares start from base * R / 2^64 and every result is
  off by a power of 2^64. bin/rsa_equiv_test_compare runs the loops'
  steps at every word count on every machine and compares rsa_vp1 with
  the 32-bit arm.

--- old
    for (size_t i = 0; i < k; i++) {
        times_word_mod(x, m, k);
    }
--- new
    for (size_t i = 0; i + 1 < k; i++) {
        times_word_mod(x, m, k);
    }
